B.cb7=new A.b7("Trend and movement","Growth / increase","A value becomes higher than its earlier or reference value.","Use \u201cincrease\u201d for a neutral change; state the comparison period and quantify it.","Revenue increased by 12% compared with the previous quarter.","","","","","An increase is not automatically favourable: higher expenses may be undesirable.",null)
B.cap=new A.b7("Trend and movement","Surged","Increased rapidly over a relatively short period.","Use when the size or rate of increase is unusually high relative to a meaningful baseline.","Monthly revenue surged by 35% following the campaign.","","","","","A surge describes movement; it does not prove what caused it.",null)
B.cbK=new A.b7("Trend and movement","Decline / decrease","A value becomes lower than its earlier or reference value.","Use for a downward movement; identify whether it is one-period change or sustained trend.","Order volume declined by 8% year over year.","","","","","",null)
B.cbE=new A.b7("Trend and movement","Stable / no change","A measure remains approximately at the same level over a stated period.","Use when variation is small relative to the measure and decision context.","Customer churn remained broadly stable at 3.2%.","","","","","Stable does not mean healthy; compare the level with a target or benchmark.",null)
B.caW=new A.b7("Trend and movement","Fluctuation","Repeated or irregular movement above and below a typical level.","Use when a series varies rather than following a smooth direction.","Daily demand fluctuated considerably during the holiday period.","","","","","",null)
B.cbr=new A.b7("Trend and movement","Peak","The highest observed value within a defined period or dataset.","State the time window or comparison set.","Daily orders peaked at 1,240 on 18 October.","","","","","",null)
B.cao=new A.b7("Trend and movement","Trough","The lowest observed value within a defined period or dataset.","Use for the low point in a time series or cycle.","Production reached a trough in the second week of June.","","","","","",null)
B.caA=new A.b7("Trend and movement","Recovery","A measure rises after a prior decline, moving toward its earlier level or target.","State whether the former level has actually been regained.","Sales recovered to 96% of their pre-disruption level.","","","","","",null)
B.cbc=new A.b7("Trend and movement","Reversal","The direction of a trend changes from rising to falling, or vice versa.","Use when direction changes, not merely when values fluctuate.","The upward sales trend reversed in the final month.","","","","","",null)
B.cbi=new A.b7("Trend and movement","Acceleration","The rate of increase becomes faster over time.","Use when successive changes show a rising growth rate, not simply a rising value.","Revenue growth accelerated from 4% to 9% across consecutive quarters.","","","","","",null)
B.cat=new A.b7("Trend and movement","Deceleration","The rate of growth or decline slows.","Use when growth continues but at a slower rate, or a decline becomes less rapid.","Subscriber growth decelerated from 14% to 6%.","","","","","",null)
B.cbD=new A.b7("Magnitude and scale","Significant","Important or large enough to matter in context; in statistics it can mean a test meets a defined threshold.","Clarify practical importance versus statistical significance.","The 2.1-point conversion improvement was commercially material.","","","","","Statistical significance is not the same as practical significance.",null)
B.caN=new A.b7("Magnitude and scale","Substantial","Large in amount or degree relative to the context.","Use for a clearly meaningful magnitude and provide the amount where possible.","The branch recorded a substantial reduction in processing time.","","","","","",null)
B.cbg=new A.b7("Magnitude and scale","Material","Large enough to influence a decision, financial statement or business judgement.","Use when the effect matters to a decision threshold or reporting context.","The cost variance is material to the quarterly operating plan.","","","","","",null)
B.caI=new A.b7("Magnitude and scale","Marginal","Small or limited in size, often close to a threshold.","Use for a small difference; do not imply statistical insignificance.","The new workflow produced a marginal increase in throughput.","","","","","",null)
B.cay=new A.b7("Magnitude and scale","Incremental","A small additional change or improvement added to an existing level.","Use for stepwise gains or additions.","The team delivered incremental productivity improvements each month.","","","","","",null)
B.cb8=new A.b7("Magnitude and scale","Negligible","So small that it has little practical effect in the stated context.","Use only when the effect is immaterial for the decision.","The rounding difference was negligible relative to total spend.","","","","","",null)
B.cbk=new A.b7("Magnitude and scale","Nominal","A face-value amount; in some contexts, an amount not adjusted for inflation.","Use carefully: nominal does not necessarily mean small.","Nominal revenue rose 5%, while inflation-adjusted revenue rose 1%.","","","","","",null)
B.cbs=new A.b7("Magnitude and scale","Proportional","Changing in a consistent ratio to another quantity.","Use when the relationship is ratio-based, not merely when values move together.","Support staffing increased proportionally with active customer volume.","","","","","",null)
B.cbj=new A.b7("Distribution and variation","Average (mean)","The arithmetic sum of values divided by the number of observations.","Use when the mean is representative and extreme values do not dominate.","Average order value was \u20b91,850.","Numeric observations","What is the arithmetic average?","Uses every value.","Sensitive to extreme observations.","",null)
B.caD=new A.b7("Distribution and variation","Median","The middle observation after values are sorted.","Use for skewed data such as salaries, transaction values or delivery times.","The median delivery time was 2.4 days.","Ordered numeric observations","What is the central observation?","Robust to extreme values.","Does not describe the full spread.","",null)
B.cbf=new A.b7("Distribution and variation","Mode","The most frequently occurring value or category.","Use to identify the most common response, product or category.","The most common ticket category was account access.","","","","","",null)
B.cbz=new A.b7("Distribution and variation","Variance","The average squared deviation from the mean, using a population or sample definition.","Use as a dispersion measure in statistical work when squared units are acceptable.","The sample variance of daily demand increased in peak season.","","","","","",null)
B.caU=new A.b7("Distribution and variation","Standard deviation","The square root of variance; describes spread around the mean in original units.","Use when mean-based spread is appropriate for the distribution.","Demand averaged 500 units with a standard deviation of 42 units.","","","","","",null)
B.cbL=new A.b7("Distribution and variation","Skewness","A measure of distribution asymmetry.","Use to describe whether a distribution has a longer tail on one side.","Transaction values were positively skewed, with a few very large orders.","","","","","Positive skew generally has a longer right tail; negative skew a longer left tail.",null)
B.caB=new A.b7("Distribution and variation","Kurtosis","A measure related to tail heaviness and extreme observations relative to a reference distribution.","Use when tail behaviour matters; state the kurtosis convention.","The return series showed elevated excess kurtosis and heavier tails.","","","","","",null)
B.cbH=new A.b7("Distribution and variation","Outlier","An observation unusually distant from the rest under a chosen rule or model.","Check data quality and context; an outlier may be valid or erroneous.","One transaction was flagged as an outlier for manual review.","","","","","",null)
B.caV=new A.b7("Distribution and variation","Quartile","One of three cut points dividing sorted data into four groups.","Use to summarize spread and compare lower, middle and upper portions.","The third quartile of resolution time was 4.8 hours.","","","","","",null)
B.cb6=new A.b7("Distribution and variation","Percentile","A value at or below which a stated percentage of observations falls.","Use for service levels, ranking and distribution thresholds.","The 90th percentile response time was 1.8 seconds.","","","","","",null)
B.cav=new A.b7("Distribution and variation","Distribution","The pattern of values, including frequency, centre, spread, shape and tails.","Use when the full pattern matters more than one summary statistic.","Customer spend followed a right-skewed distribution.","","","","","",null)
B.caY=new A.b7("Distribution and variation","Deviation","The difference between an observation and a reference value, often the mean or target.","Always state the reference point; distinguish deviation from standard deviation.","Actual cost deviated by \u20b942,000 from budget.","","","","","",null)
B.cb5=new A.b7("Performance and evaluation","Outperformed","Achieved a better result than a defined comparator.","Name the benchmark or peer group and ensure like-for-like scope.","The East branch outperformed the regional average on on-time delivery.","","","","","",null)
B.caP=new A.b7("Performance and evaluation","Underperformed","Achieved a result below a defined expectation, benchmark or peer reference.","Use with a clear comparator and fair, like-for-like scope.","The branch underperformed its quarterly sales target by 7%.","","","","","",null)
B.caw=new A.b7("Performance and evaluation","Exceeded expectations","Delivered a result better than the agreed expectation or target.","Use when the expectation was defined before observing the result.","Retention exceeded the 92% target, reaching 94.1%.","","","","","",null)
B.caM=new A.b7("Performance and evaluation","Fell short","Did not reach a stated target or expected level.","Use for a measurable gap against an explicit goal.","The project fell short of its 30-day completion target.","","","","","",null)
B.cax=new A.b7("Performance and evaluation","Optimal","Best under a stated objective and constraints; not universally best.","State the objective and relevant constraints.","The schedule was optimal for minimizing overtime while meeting demand.","","","","","",null)
B.caE=new A.b7("Performance and evaluation","Suboptimal","Not the best available result under the stated objective and constraints.","Use when a better feasible alternative exists or performance is below an agreed standard.","The current allocation is suboptimal during peak-hour demand.","","","","","",null)
B.caH=new A.b7("Performance and evaluation","Favorable","A variance or outcome that benefits the stated objective.","Interpret direction in context: lower cost may be favourable; lower revenue is not.","Operating expenses were \u20b91.2 lakh below budget, a favourable variance.","","","","","",null)
B.cb3=new A.b7("Performance and evaluation","Adverse","An outcome or variance that works against the stated objective.","Use with the relevant target or business consequence.","An adverse cost variance widened during the quarter.","","","","","",null)
B.caR=new A.b7("Performance and evaluation","Efficiency","Output achieved relative to inputs consumed.","Use an explicit ratio such as units per labour hour or cost per transaction.","Processing efficiency improved to 18 cases per employee-hour.","","","","","",null)
B.caZ=new A.b7("Performance and evaluation","Productivity","The amount of output produced per unit of input over a period.","Compare output and resource input using consistent definitions.","Team productivity increased from 24 to 28 completed cases per week.","","","","","",null)
B.cbw=new A.b7("Comparison and context","Year-over-Year (YoY)","Compares a period with the corresponding period one year earlier.","Use to reduce seasonal distortion in annual business cycles.","October revenue grew 9% YoY.","","","","","",null)
B.cb0=new A.b7("Comparison and context","Month-over-Month (MoM)","Compares a month with the immediately preceding month.","Use for short-term movement; account for month length and seasonality.","Active users increased 3.5% MoM.","","","","","",null)
B.cbF=new A.b7("Comparison and context","Quarter-over-Quarter (QoQ)","Compares one fiscal or calendar quarter with the immediately preceding quarter.","Disclose the fiscal-quarter convention.","Gross margin improved 1.4 percentage points QoQ.","","","","","",null)
B.cbo=new A.b7("Comparison and context","Period-over-Period","Compares a defined reporting period with the prior comparable period.","State the exact period pair.","Returns fell 6% period over period.","","","","","",null)
B.cbJ=new A.b7("Comparison and context","Benchmark","A reference standard, peer group or external comparator.","Choose a relevant, current comparator measured consistently.","The branch conversion rate was 2.3 points below the industry benchmark.","","","","","",null)
B.caJ=new A.b7("Comparison and context","Baseline","The starting or reference measurement against which later results are assessed.","Define date, scope and calculation method.","The project baseline was 14 days per onboarding case.","","","","","",null)
B.car=new A.b7("Comparison and context","Relative change","Change expressed as a proportion or percentage of the starting value.","Use (new \u2212 old) \xf7 old \xd7 100 and state the base period.","Revenue increased 30%, from \u20b910 lakh to \u20b913 lakh.","","","","","",null)
B.caF=new A.b7("Comparison and context","Absolute change","The arithmetic difference between two values, in original units.","Use to communicate the actual amount added or lost.","Revenue increased by \u20b93 lakh, from \u20b910 lakh to \u20b913 lakh.","","","","","",null)
B.cba=new A.b7("Comparison and context","Variance analysis","Examines the difference between actual and budget, forecast, target or prior period.","Quantify the gap and investigate its components.","Actual operating cost was \u20b92.4 lakh above budget.","","","","","",null)
B.cbl=new A.b7("Relationships and causes","Correlation","A statistical measure of direction and strength of association between variables.","Choose Pearson, Spearman or another method to suit the data.","Ad spend and sales showed a positive correlation.","Paired numeric observations","Do variables co-move?","Summarizes association.","Correlation alone does not establish causation.","",null)
B.cbA=new A.b7("Relationships and causes","Association","A general relationship or dependence between variables or categories.","Use when describing a relationship without asserting a causal mechanism.","Late deliveries were associated with lower customer satisfaction.","","","","","",null)
B.cb1=new A.b7("Relationships and causes","Positive correlation","Two variables tend to move in the same direction.","Use when higher values of one tend to accompany higher values of another.","Order volume and packing hours had a positive correlation.","","","","","",null)
B.caG=new A.b7("Relationships and causes","Negative correlation","Two variables tend to move in opposite directions.","Use when higher values of one tend to accompany lower values of another.","Wait time and satisfaction showed a negative correlation.","","","","","",null)
B.cbv=new A.b7("Relationships and causes","Causation","A change in one factor produces a change in another under a defensible causal design.","Require credible evidence such as a randomized experiment or robust quasi-experiment.","A controlled experiment estimated that reminders caused a 4-point lift in attendance.","","","","","",null)
B.cbe=new A.b7("Relationships and causes","Contributing factor","A condition that may help explain an outcome, often alongside other factors.","Use for plausible influences while causal evidence is being assessed.","Staffing shortages were a contributing factor in delayed dispatches.","","","","","",null)
B.caS=new A.b7("Relationships and causes","Driver","A variable or operational factor that materially influences a result.","Use when evidence supports influence; otherwise say candidate driver.","Repeat-purchase frequency was a key revenue driver.","","","","","",null)
B.caX=new A.b7("Relationships and causes","Impact","The effect or consequence associated with a change, action or event.","Quantify the outcome and distinguish estimated impact from observed difference.","The policy change reduced average handling time by 11%.","","","","","",null)
B.cby=new A.b7("Relationships and causes","Dependency","A condition or variable on which another process or outcome relies.","Use for operational, technical or analytical prerequisites.","Forecast accuracy depends on complete, consistently dated sales history.","","","","","",null)
B.cau=new A.b7("Relationships and causes","Attribution","A method of assigning credit or contribution to touchpoints, factors or sources.","Name the attribution model and its assumptions.","Last-click attribution assigned 42% of conversions to paid search.","","","","","",null)
B.cbI=new A.b7("Forecasting and prediction","Projection","A calculated future value based on stated assumptions or an extrapolated pattern.","Make assumptions explicit; treat the result as conditional.","At the current run rate, the projection is \u20b91.8 crore for the year.","","","","","",null)
B.cb2=new A.b7("Forecasting and prediction","Forecast","An estimate of a future outcome using history, assumptions and a model.","Use when estimating the most plausible future under current information.","The demand forecast indicates 8,500 units next month.","","","","","",null)
B.caC=new A.b7("Forecasting and prediction","Extrapolation","Extending an observed pattern beyond the range of available data.","Use cautiously when the underlying process is reasonably stable.","A straight-line extrapolation suggests further growth if conditions persist.","","","","","",null)
B.caz=new A.b7("Forecasting and prediction","Trendline","A fitted line or curve summarizing the general direction of data.","Use to show a broad pattern, not a guaranteed future path.","The trendline indicates a gradual rise in monthly demand.","","","","","",null)
B.cb9=new A.b7("Forecasting and prediction","Seasonality","A recurring pattern tied to a known calendar or seasonal cycle.","Use when periodic effects repeat at a regular interval.","Sales peak each festive quarter.","","","","","",null)
B.cbC=new A.b7("Forecasting and prediction","Moving average","An average recalculated over a rolling window of recent observations.","State the window; use to smooth noise while retaining broad direction.","The 7-day moving average reduced daily demand volatility.","","","","","",null)
B.caK=new A.b7("Forecasting and prediction","Confidence interval","An interval procedure that captures a fixed parameter at a stated coverage rate under repeated sampling assumptions.","Use for an estimated parameter; distinguish from a prediction interval for future observations.","The estimated lift was 2.4 points with a 95% confidence interval of 0.8\u20134.0 points.","","","","","",null)
B.cbu=new A.b7("Forecasting and prediction","Prediction","An estimated value or class for a new or future case.","Communicate uncertainty and validation performance.","The model predicts elevated renewal risk for this account.","","","","","",null)
B.caL=new A.b7("Forecasting and prediction","Scenario analysis","Compares outcomes under different internally consistent assumptions.","Use when future conditions are uncertain and decisions depend on alternatives.","The downside scenario assumes 10% lower demand and 5% higher input costs.","","","","","",null)
B.cbq=new A.b7("Data quality and reliability","Completeness","The extent to which required records and fields are present.","State denominator and required-field definition.","Customer email completeness was 97.6%.","","","","","",null)
B.cas=new A.b7("Data quality and reliability","Accuracy","How closely recorded values match true or accepted reference values.","Use when values can be checked against a trusted source.","A sample audit found 99.2% accuracy in invoice amounts.","","","","","",null)
B.cbn=new A.b7("Data quality and reliability","Consistency","Whether values and formats follow the same rules across records and systems.","Use for standardized definitions, units, codes and formats.","Date formats were inconsistent across source files.","","","","","",null)
B.caO=new A.b7("Data quality and reliability","Validity","Whether values conform to defined rules, ranges, formats or business constraints.","Use for rule-based checks; valid data can still be inaccurate.","All invoice dates passed permitted date-range validation.","","","","","",null)
B.cbx=new A.b7("Data quality and reliability","Uniqueness","Whether each entity or event appears only as intended, without unintended duplicates.","Define the unique key or duplicate-detection rule.","Customer IDs were unique after duplicate resolution.","","","","","",null)
B.cbG=new A.b7("Data quality and reliability","Missing values","Fields for which no value is recorded or available.","Report count and percentage; assess missingness before imputation.","Eleven percent of records lacked a verified region.","","","","","",null)
B.caQ=new A.b7("Data quality and reliability","Duplicate records","Multiple rows representing the same entity or event under the chosen matching rule.","Define the entity key and distinguish duplicates from legitimate repeated events.","Duplicate invoice IDs accounted for 0.7% of imported rows.","","","","","",null)
B.cbp=new A.b7("Data quality and reliability","Data integrity","The degree to which data remains accurate, complete, consistent and protected through its lifecycle.","Use for end-to-end trustworthiness, constraints and controlled transformations.","Referential checks and audit logs helped preserve data integrity.","","","","","",null)
